bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    optional_return_into_scalar_fn_accepted_2026-11-26, 0, "Typed-return contract break. fn value() -> i64: return maybe() (maybe: -> i64?) and return map.get(1) (Dict.get is V? since 9d21958ee39) both compile and run on the seed: simple check emits 'warning: declared return type mismatch admitted (seed aggregate typing not authoritative)' and passes; simple run exits 0 printing a heap word (aarch64 2026-11-26: 6057657724097, 5904280416257). Expected: a return type mismatch error (expected i64, found i64?). simple check (pure-Simple checker) rejects the explicit i64? form but PASSES the Dict.get form, so the checker needs the fix too. With a seed HIR reject the JIT demotes to the interpreter, which prints 7 and exits 0, the same as the float->int return precedent. Red in-development spec: check_optional_return_into_scalar_spec.spl (2 red + 1 green control)."

